## ⚠️ Edge case — reversing lift BOM kitted gap (WHY + how to resolve)

**Finding (named):** several recent BOM imports have parts in `parts_control` but **0 build-pack GIDs assigned** (not kitted):

| Project | BOM lines | parts_control | open | with pack GID |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **1595 St Georges** | 235 | 225 | 189 | **0** ← worst |
| **1365 Serjeants Inn** | 10 | **0** | — | **0** ← parts absent |
| **1037 (Long/Lower)** | 3 | 52 | 24 | **0** |

**Likely root cause:** the BOM import (Stage 5) creates Project-Order/vendor tasks, but the **build-pack association step never ran** — `parts_control.build_assembly_pack_gid` stays NULL and `association_status` unlinked. This is the same family as the 1588 phantom-GID / kitting gap. Whether it's specifically the "reversing lift" (1578 Traversing / a reversing-drive scissor) needs Giles's confirmation — the imported projects with zero kit are clearly 1595/1365/1037.

**How to resolve:** run the **`legacy_bom_pack_allocation`** flow (`legacy_bom_pack_ingest.py --scan` then reviewed `--commit`) to assign each imported part's verified Build Schedule pack GID to `parts_control` + the Asana Build Packs reference field. This is exactly the same pipeline as the *legacy BOM push* flagged for tomorrow morning — the un-kitted parts ARE the "no items kitted" edge case.

